    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch06-19: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.78";
    dc:description "Specific self-emulation identities and rule 90's nested form are exactly checkable. The asserted dichotomy needs formal qualifications and is doubtful over the full stated scope, so only the intended restricted version is resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/proof";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Formalize self-emulation as a block map commuting with the cellular-automaton evolution, then prove that repeated rescaling constrains configurations to uniform or self-similar nested forms under the intended assumptions. Search finite rule and block spaces for a self-emulating counterexample with another morphology.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Self-simulation can support complex behavior in broader automaton classes.", "The claim omits assumptions on the block map and initial condition.", "“Nested” lacks a single formal definition.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.72"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch06-19--gpt--dataset-1>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.779"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
